# Command Execution

## NEVER Run These Commands
- **`bun start`**: NEVER run the bot in production mode
- **`bun dev`**: NEVER run the bot in development mode
- **`bun prisma migrate dev`**: NEVER create migrations
- **`bun prisma migrate deploy`**: NEVER deploy migrations
- **`bun prisma db push`**: NEVER push schema changes directly to database
- **`bun prisma db pull`**: NEVER pull schema from database
- **`bun prisma studio`**: NEVER open Prisma Studio

## The ONLY Prisma Command Allowed
- **`bun prisma generate`**: ONLY allowed command after editing `prisma/schema.prisma`
  - Run this immediately after any changes to the Prisma schema
  - This regenerates the Prisma client with updated types

## What Cursor Should Do
- Edit code files normally
- Make schema changes in `prisma/schema.prisma`
- Run `bun prisma generate` after schema changes
- Never assume the user wants to start/stop the bot
- Never create or modify migrations
- Let the user control bot execution and database migrations manually

## Rationale
- Bot execution should be controlled by the user in their terminal
- Migrations require user decision and context
- Prisma client generation is the only safe automated operation
- Avoid interfering with the user's development workflow
